endobj
243 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (6.1. Overview)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Data is collected by dedicated Python scripts for the four live sources: REST API calls for Jooble, JSearch, and FreeHire, and a scraper for Tanqeeb. Tapneo is imported manually as a one-time load. The Jooble and FreeHire scripts retry with exponential backoff on transient server errors \(429, 500, 502, 503, 504\), while JSearch and Tanqeeb log failures and skip to the next request. )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Raw data is first written to Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2, organized by source and ingestion date \(e.g., raw/<source>/ingest_date=<date>/data.json\). This preserves the original data for auditability and reprocessing.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (From there, data is loaded into Snowflake with COPY INTO, populating a raw \(Bronze\) layer with one table per source \(e.g., RAW_JOOBLE_JOBS\). Snowflake tracks which files were already loaded, so re-runs do not create duplicates.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (The pipeline draws on five distinct sources to ensure broad and reliable coverage of the Saudi Arabian tech job market, combining official APIs, web scraping, and a static historical dataset.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Jooble is accessed through its official API, using an authenticated POST request with a custom API key. Data is returned in JSON format, providing structured, reliable job listings.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
249 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (JSearch is accessed via RapidAPI using a standard GET request. It returns data in both CSV and JSON formats and offers broad international job coverage, including postings relevant to the Saudi market.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
250 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (FreeHire is accessed through a direct API request made via the browser, returning JSON-formatted job data from its endpoint.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Tapneo differs from the other sources in that it is not queried live. Instead, a static dataset is downloaded once and read directly using Pandas. This source serves as a historical baseline rather than an ongoing feed, since no live extraction script exists for it.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 133 0 R
/E (Tanqeeb, specifically the Saudi Arabia section of the site, does not provide a public API. Data from this source is therefore collected through web scraping, using BeautifulSoup in combination with a ScrapeOps proxy to handle JavaScript rendering and avoid blocking. Data returned is semi-structured JSON.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
