263 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (The pipeline follows a pull-based batch model: each source is queried on demand or on a schedule, rather than receiving continuous pushes. This was chosen because:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 970 0 R
/E (All sources expose request/response APIs or scrapeable pages, not event streams or webhooks.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
265 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 971 0 R
/E (Job postings are low-frequency data, so batch pulls capture new records without unnecessary API usage.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
266 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 972 0 R
/E (Batch ingestion fits the Bronze-Silver-Gold model, where each run produces a traceable, timestamped raw snapshot.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (6.3. Pagination Handling)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (Each source is queried with a strategy suited to its API and rate limits:)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
269 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/E (6.4. Error Handling and Rate Limiting)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
270 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 973 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
