435 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 143 0 R
/E (This file transforms the `skills` column \(a single text string containing multiple comma-separated skills\) into a separate row for each skill. Here is a real-world example of the issue we resolved: without standardization, "Google Cloud" appeared in the data in three distinct forms \(`gcp`: 43 times; `google cloud`: 17 times; `google cloud platform`: 7 times\). Consequently, any analysis of the "most in-demand skill" would have obscured its true prevalence \(67 total occurrences\). We solved this using a seed file \(`skill_synonyms.csv`\) that maps each variation to a standardized name.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
