470 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1075 0 R
/E (Consistent job_posting_key : The job_posting_key is generated using the same five attributes that define the job grain: company, city, country, location, and title. This ensures consistent identification and prevents potential key collisions between fct_job_postings and fct_job_skills.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
471 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1076 0 R
/E (Conformed Dimensions : Shared dimension keys \(company_key, location_key, job_attributes_key, and date_key\) are included in both fact tables. This allows skills to be analyzed directly by company, location, job attributes, and date without requiring direct fact-to-fact joins.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
472 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1077 0 R
/E (Unknown Member Pattern for Missing Values : Missing attributes are retained rather than removing incomplete records. Standardized values such as Unknown Company and Not Specified, along with an appropriate unknown date member, are used to preserve the complete job record while making missing information explicit and analyzable.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
