482 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (The five tables loaded into Snowflake from Python flow into five stg_*.sql staging models, where columns are standardized without applying major business transformations. The data is then combined through int_all_jobs using UNION ALL, followed by int_jobs_deduplicated, which establishes the job grain using five attributes: company, city, country, location, and title.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
483 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (The deduplicated data then flows into int_jobs_enriched, where additional business attributes such as seniority_level and job_category are derived. From this point, the data branches into the dimension models and the skill-processing path. The dimension models support fct_job_postings, while int_job_skills processes individual skills and their normalized synonyms before feeding dim_skill and fct_job_skills.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
484 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 146 0 R
/E (dim_date appears separately in the dbt lineage graph because it is generated using a date_spine rather than being derived through a ref\(\) relationship from the source data. Its functional relationship with the fact tables is nevertheless established through the corresponding date keys and validated using successful relationships tests.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
