/E (13.4 UNDERSTANDING THE JOB-SKILL RELATIONSHIPS)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
555 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (The relationship between job postings and technical skills is represented by 7,883 records in FCT_JOB_SKILLS. These records should not be interpreted as 7,883 unique skills. Instead, they represent individual relationships between a job posting and a skill. Since one job can require multiple skills, the number of job-skill relationships is expected to be greater than the number of unique job postings or unique skills.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
556 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 151 0 R
/E (For example, a single job posting may be associated with Python, SQL, AWS, and Docker. Each association is represented as a separate job-skill relationship, while each technology itself appears only once in the DIM_SKILL dimension.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
557 0 obj
<<
